{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "3: Live updates",
  "description": "End-to-end: how a Copilot database write or a Claude transcript append becomes a near-real-time refresh of the desktop's live board, coalesced behind one debounce. Every step embeds the numbered sequence diagram and points at the exact code for that step.",
  "nextTour": "5: Workflow deviation markers",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — Watch Copilot's database",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/live/liveBoard.ts",
      "line": 331,
      "description": "![3: Live updates](.tours/diagrams/d-19.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 1 of 6 in the sequence diagram — `Copilot DB → LiveBoardService: DB / WAL file change`**\n\nThe live board watches Copilot's database and its `-wal` file as plain files. Nothing is installed into Copilot — no hooks, no exporters — because it already writes these files. Nothing leaves the machine."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — Signal, don't refresh",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/live/liveBoard.ts",
      "line": 333,
      "description": "![3: Live updates](.tours/diagrams/d-20.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 2 of 6 in the sequence diagram — `LiveBoardService → LiveUpdateController: signal()`**\n\nEach change arms a quiet-period re-index and calls `controller.signal()` to say new activity arrived. The watcher never recomputes anything itself."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — The other producer signals too",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/live/claudeWatcher.ts",
      "line": 68,
      "description": "![3: Live updates](.tours/diagrams/d-21.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 3 of 6 in the sequence diagram — `ClaudeWatcher → LiveUpdateController: file change → signal()`**\n\n`ClaudeWatcher` watches Claude's transcript directories. Each filesystem event calls the same `signal()` — so Copilot writes and Claude file appends feed one controller, not competing refresh loops. The Copilot CLI and JetBrains stores register the same way."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Coalesce with one debounce",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/live/liveUpdateController.ts",
      "line": 65,
      "description": "![3: Live updates](.tours/diagrams/d-22.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 4 of 6 in the sequence diagram — `LiveUpdateController → LiveBoardService: debounced onRefresh`**\n\n`LiveUpdateController.signal` folds a burst of signals into a single debounced flush (`LIVE_DEBOUNCE_MS`, 750 ms on the desktop), so a storm of span commits or file appends becomes one `recompute` instead of hundreds."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5 — Quiet-period re-index",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/live/liveBoard.ts",
      "line": 312,
      "description": "![3: Live updates](.tours/diagrams/d-23.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 5 of 6 in the sequence diagram — `LiveBoardService → Index pass: requestIndex()`**\n\nOnce the files have been quiet for a moment, `armReindex` asks for an index pass (flow 1) so the Sessions list and the dashboard pick up the change without a manual Refresh. The request is never awaited: the board's own status comes from the transcript tail."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 6 — Push and repaint",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/renderer/src/views/workspace/useLiveBoard.ts",
      "line": 25,
      "description": "![3: Live updates](.tours/diagrams/d-24.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 6 of 6 in the sequence diagram — `LiveBoardService → Workspace view: workspace.live snapshot`**\n\n`recompute` re-derives each session's status and emits a `workspace.live` event only when something really changed. The renderer's `useLiveBoard` hook swaps in the new snapshot and the live board repaints in near-real-time."
    }
  ]
}
